{
  "title": "Pulse-pressure\u2013pulse coupling adds no demonstrated albuminuria prediction gain across NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "In 3,063 NHANES 2005\u20132006 adults and 4,863 separately sampled 2009\u20132010 adults, adding pulse-pressure \u00d7 radial-pulse coupling to flexible marginal hemodynamic and clinical predictors yielded no demonstrated improvement in concurrent log urine ACR prediction: target weighted MSE difference -0.00012677 (-0.0164%); full source-plus-target bootstrap 95% interval [-0.004552, 0.003790]. This does not rule out physiological association or longitudinal prognostic value.",
  "keywords": [
    "pulsatile stress",
    "albuminuria",
    "NHANES",
    "incremental prediction",
    "negative result"
  ],
